1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,443
Hey, I'm Nova. In the next two minutes,
we'll compare machine learning with deep
learning and see what each is good at.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,883
AI is the broad goal. Machine learning is
one way computers learn patterns from
examples instead of following every hand-
written rule.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,138
Give a model many labeled cat and dog
photos. It learns patterns from those
examples, then uses them to classify new
pictures.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,208
In traditional machine learning, people
choose features such as ear shape, fur
color, body outline, and size before
training.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,533
Deep learning is a type of machine learning.
Layered neural networks learn useful
features directly from raw data, including
images and sound.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,658
Early layers detect edges and shapes. Later
layers combine them into patterns like
whiskers, eyes, faces, and objects.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,363
This helps analyze images, speech, and
video, powering tools for medical scans,
face recognition, and driver assistance.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,288
Deep learning often needs more data and
computing power. Traditional machine
learning can be faster and easier to
inspect.

9
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,753
For a small dataset and clear features,
start with a machine-learning baseline. It
might already solve the problem well.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,958
For complicated patterns and plenty of
examples, deep learning may perform better.
It still needs careful training and fair
testing.

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,973
Compare both on data the model has never
seen. Check accuracy, reliability, cost, and
the mistakes each approach makes.

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:57,983
Deep learning is part of machine learning.
Both learn from data. Choose the simplest
method that reliably solves your task.
